ASSET DESCRIPTION [Insert a detailed description of the underlying asset.]


LSI is a distributor of electrical cable and accessories primarily servicing the energy industry, with most of its business being derived from the sale of “Exane” brand electric cable to oil drilling rig manufacturers and refurbishers.  The Company was originally founded in 1974 and changed ownership in 1993 during a liquidation of non-core business subsidiaries by Weatherford International.  The Company’s competitive advantage derives from its exclusive distributorship arrangement with the Rockbestos Surprenant Cable Corporation that is the manufacturer of “Exane” cable, the most popular brand of electrical cable in the drilling industry.










